lambda: (Bytes, Array[(String, Option[TypeExpr])], Expr, Array[String], Int, CompileCtx, Int, (Bytes, Expr, Array[String], Int, CompileCtx, Int) -> Int with { Error }) -> Int with { Error } = (buf, params, fn_body, local_names, next_local, ctx, ld, compile_fn) -> {\\n  let param_names_arr = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  let mut pi = 0\\n  while pi < Array::length(params) {\\n    let (pname, _) = Array::get(params, pi)\\n    Array::push(param_names_arr, pname)\\n    pi = pi + 1\\n  }\\n  let fn_and_ctor = Array::concat(ctx.func_table.names, ctx.ctor_table.names)\\n  let captures = collect_free_vars(fn_body, param_names_arr, fn_and_ctor)\\n  let num_captures = Array::length(captures)\\n  let user_params = Array::length(params)\\n  let lam_buf = bytebuf_new()\\n  let lam_locals = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  let mut lpi = 0\\n  while lpi < user_params {\\n    let (lpname_raw, _) = Array::get(params, lpi)\\n    let lpnlen = String::length(lpname_raw)\\n    let lpname = if lpnlen > 0 {\\n      let lpc = String::char_code_at(lpname_raw, lpnlen - 1)\\n      if lpc == '~' {\\n        lpname_raw[0: lpnlen - 1]\\n      } else if lpc == '?' {\\n        lpname_raw[0: lpnlen - 1]\\n      } else {\\n        lpname_raw\\n      }\\n    } else lpname_raw\\n    Array::push(lam_locals, lpname)\\n    lpi = lpi + 1\\n  }\\n  Array::push(lam_locals, \\\"__env\\\")\\n  let env_param_idx = user_params\\n  let lam_nl_start = user_params + 1\\n  let lam_ref_cells = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  let mut ci3 = 0\\n  let mut lam_nl = lam_nl_start\\n  while ci3 < num_captures {\\n    let cap_local = lam_nl\\n    let cap_name = Array::get(captures, ci3)\\n    emit_local_get(lam_buf, env_param_idx)\\n    emit_i32_wrap_i64(lam_buf)\\n    emit_i64_load(lam_buf, 3, 8 + ci3 * 8)\\n    // #699: a captured RC ref cell is stored odd-tagged in the env (so the\\n    // closure's class-7 drop classifies and frees it). The inner body uses the\\n    // cell as an even vptr (load/store at +0), so untag on load back.\\n    if ctx.enable_rc && array_contains_str(ctx.ref_cell_names, cap_name) {\\n      emit_i64_const(lam_buf, -2)\\n      emit_i64_and(lam_buf)\\n    }\\n    emit_local_set(lam_buf, cap_local)\\n    Array::push(lam_locals, cap_name)\\n    if array_contains_str(ctx.ref_cell_names, cap_name) {\\n      Array::push(lam_ref_cells, cap_name)\\n    } else {\\n      ()\\n    }\\n    // #705: a captured non-refcell heap var is a BORROWED view of the defining\\n    // scope's binding — the env store (below) does NOT bump its rc, and the\\n    // body's perceus plan never tracks a free var, so any owning consume inside\\n    // the closure decrements a refcount the closure does not own. Left unbalanced\\n    // that frees the defining scope's value early (double free / heap cycle when\\n    // a recursive closure consumes a captured list each iteration — e.g. a set\\n    // op's `contains(b, head)` over a borrowed `b`). Dup the capture once per\\n    // owning consume here in the prologue: it runs per invocation, so a recursive\\n    // closure consuming the capture each call stays balanced (defining scope\\n    // still drops it exactly once). Ref-cell captures (#699) own their cell via\\n    // the env store and are reclaimed by the closure's class-7 drop; skip them.\\n    if ctx.enable_rc && !array_contains_str(ctx.ref_cell_names, cap_name) {\\n      let cap_consumes = md_consume_count(fn_body, cap_name)\\n      let mut cdup = 0\\n      while cdup < cap_consumes {\\n        emit_rc_dup_guarded(lam_buf, cap_local, ctx.rc_shadow)\\n        cdup = cdup + 1\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      ()\\n    }\\n    lam_nl = lam_nl + 1\\n    ci3 = ci3 + 1\\n  }\\n  let norm_params = Array::slice(params, 0, 0)\\n  let mut npi = 0\\n  while npi < Array::length(params) {\\n    let (rawn, pty) = Array::get(params, npi)\\n    let rnlen = String::length(rawn)\\n    let sn = if rnlen > 0 {\\n      let lc = String::char_code_at(rawn, rnlen - 1)\\n      if lc == '~' || lc == '?' {\\n        rawn[0: rnlen - 1]\\n      } else {\\n        rawn\\n      }\\n    } else {\\n      rawn\\n    }\\n    Array::push(norm_params, (sn, pty))\\n    npi = npi + 1\\n  }\\n  let lam_drops = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  let lam_alias_dups = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  let lam_dups = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  let lam_heap_params = Array::slice([\\n    \\\"\\\"\\n  ], 0, 0)\\n  if ctx.enable_rc {\\n    let lam_plan = build_perceus_plan_with_params(norm_params, fn_body, ctx.borrow_ret_names)\\n    let mut ldi = 0\\n    while ldi < Array::length(lam_plan) {\\n      let lpa = Array::get(lam_plan, ldi)\\n      if pa_is_drop(lpa) {\\n        Array::push(lam_drops, lpa.name)\\n      } else if pa_is_alias_dup(lpa) {\\n        Array::push(lam_alias_dups, lpa.name)\\n      } else if pa_is_dup(lpa) {\\n        Array::push(lam_dups, lpa.name)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      ldi = ldi + 1\\n    }\\n    let mut hpi = 0\\n    while hpi < Array::length(norm_params) {\\n      let (hpn, hpt) = Array::get(norm_params, hpi)\\n      if param_is_heap_in_body(hpn, hpt, fn_body) {\\n        Array::push(lam_heap_params, hpn)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      hpi = hpi + 1\\n    }\\n  }\\n  let lam_ctx = CompileCtx::{\\n    func_table: ctx.func_table, str_table: ctx.str_table,\\n    lambda_table: ctx.lambda_table,\\n    num_user_funcs: ctx.num_user_funcs, func_offset: ctx.func_offset,\\n    ref_cell_names: lam_ref_cells, ctor_table: ctx.ctor_table,\\n    thunk_names: ctx.thunk_names,\\n    const_int_names: ctx.const_int_names,\\n    const_int_values: ctx.const_int_values,\\n    enable_rc: ctx.enable_rc,\\n    rc_shadow: ctx.rc_shadow,\\n    rc_drop_names: lam_drops,\\n    rc_alias_dup_names: lam_alias_dups,\\n    heap_binding_names: lam_heap_params,\\n    rc_drop_func_idx: ctx.rc_drop_func_idx,\\n    rc_alloc_func_idx: ctx.rc_alloc_func_idx,\\n    heap_grow_check_func_idx: ctx.heap_grow_check_func_idx,\\n    rc_dup_names: lam_dups,\\n    float_local_slots: Array::slice([\\n      0\\n    ], 0, 0),\\n    int_local_slots: Array::slice([\\n      0\\n    ], 0, 0),\\n    effect_names: ctx.effect_names,\\n    effect_op_keys: ctx.effect_op_keys,\\n    effect_op_arities: ctx.effect_op_arities,\\n    cov: ctx.cov,\\n    dbg_line_idx: ctx.dbg_line_idx,\\n    dbg_line_nl: ctx.dbg_line_nl,\\n    dbg_line_file_id: ctx.dbg_line_file_id,\\n    loop_borrowed_names: Array::slice([\\n      \\\"\\\"\\n    ], 0, 0),\\n    loop_consumed_names: Array::slice([\\n      \\\"\\\"\\n    ], 0, 0),\\n    borrow_ret_names: ctx.borrow_ret_names,\\n    scalar_ret_names: ctx.scalar_ret_names\\n  }\\n  if ctx.enable_rc {\\n    let mut dpi = 0\\n    while dpi < Array::length(norm_params) {\\n      let (dpn, dpt) = Array::get(norm_params, dpi)\\n      if param_is_heap_in_body(dpn, dpt, fn_body) {\\n        let mut dcount = 0\\n        let mut dqi = 0\\n        while dqi < Array::length(lam_dups) {\\n          if Array::get(lam_dups, dqi) == dpn {\\n            dcount = dcount + 1\\n          } else {\\n            ()\\n          }\\n          dqi = dqi + 1\\n        }\\n        let mut de = 0\\n        while de < dcount {\\n          emit_rc_dup_guarded(lam_buf, dpi, ctx.rc_shadow)\\n          de = de + 1\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      dpi = dpi + 1\\n    }\\n  } else {\\n    ()\\n  }\\n  let final_lam_nl = compile_fn(lam_buf, fn_body, lam_locals, lam_nl, lam_ctx, -1)\\n  let mut tail_lam_nl = final_lam_nl\\n  if ctx.enable_rc && ctx.rc_drop_func_idx >= 0 {\\n    let tail_root = scope_tail_proj_root(fn_body)\\n    let mut need_dup = false\\n    let mut ti = 0\\n    while ti < Array::length(norm_params) {\\n      let (tpn, tpt) = Array::get(norm_params, ti)\\n      if param_is_heap_in_body(tpn, tpt, fn_body) && array_contains_str(lam_drops, tpn) && tpn == tail_root {\\n        need_dup = true\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      ti = ti + 1\\n    }\\n    let rtemp = final_lam_nl\\n    if need_dup {\\n      emit_local_set(lam_buf, rtemp)\\n      emit_rc_dup_guarded(lam_buf, rtemp, ctx.rc_shadow)\\n      tail_lam_nl = final_lam_nl + 1\\n    } else {\\n      ()\\n    }\\n    let mut tj = 0\\n    while tj < Array::length(norm_params) {\\n      let (dpn2, dpt2) = Array::get(norm_params, tj)\\n      if param_is_heap_in_body(dpn2, dpt2, fn_body) && array_contains_str(lam_drops, dpn2) {\\n        emit_local_get(lam_buf, tj)\\n        emit_call(lam_buf, ctx.rc_drop_func_idx)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      tj = tj + 1\\n    }\\n    if need_dup {\\n      emit_local_get(lam_buf, rtemp)\\n    } else {\\n      ()\\n    }\\n  } else {\\n    ()\\n  }\\n  let lambda_idx = Array::length(ctx.lambda_table.bodies)\\n  Array::push(ctx.lambda_table.bodies, lam_buf)\\n  Array::push(ctx.lambda_table.param_counts, user_params + 1)\\n  Array::push(ctx.lambda_table.captures, captures)\\n  let mut extra_lam = 0\\n  let min_lam_nl = user_params + 1\\n  if tail_lam_nl > min_lam_nl {\\n    extra_lam = tail_lam_nl - min_lam_nl\\n  }\\n  Array::push(ctx.lambda_table.meta_i32, 0)\\n  Array::push(ctx.lambda_table.meta_i64, extra_lam)\\n  let table_slot = ctx.num_user_funcs + lambda_idx\\n  if num_captures == 0 {\\n    emit_i64_const(buf, (table_slot<<2)|2)\\n    next_local\\n  } else {\\n    let ptr_local = next_local\\n    let nl2 = next_local + 1\\n    Array::push(local_names, \\\"__closure_ptr\\\")\\n    let cap_off = if ctx.enable_rc {\\n      16\\n    } else {\\n      8\\n    }\\n    if ctx.enable_rc {\\n      let total = 16 + num_captures * 8\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, total)\\n      emit_call(buf, ctx.rc_alloc_func_idx)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, total)\\n      emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 0)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, 1)\\n      emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 4)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, 7)\\n      emit_i32_store8(buf, 0, 7)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, table_slot)\\n      emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 8)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, num_captures)\\n      emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 12)\\n    } else {\\n      emit_global_get(buf, 0)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_u(buf)\\n      emit_local_tee(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, 8 + num_captures * 8)\\n      emit_i32_add(buf)\\n      emit_global_set(buf, 0)\\n      emit_heap_grow_after_heap_set(buf, ctx)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, table_slot)\\n      emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 0)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, num_captures)\\n      emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 4)\\n    }\\n    let mut csi = 0\\n    while csi < num_captures {\\n      let cap_name = Array::get(captures, csi)\\n      let mut __cap_resolve = -1\\n      let mut __cri = Array::length(local_names) - 1\\n      while __cri >= 0 {\\n        if Array::get(local_names, __cri) == cap_name {\\n          __cap_resolve = __cri\\n          __cri = -1\\n        } else {\\n          __cri = __cri - 1\\n        }\\n      }\\n      if __cap_resolve >= 0 {\\n        if ctx.enable_rc && array_contains_str(ctx.ref_cell_names, cap_name) {\\n          // #699: own the captured RC ref cell. Store it odd-tagged so the\\n          // closure's class-7 drop (gen_rc_drop_body) recognises it as an owned\\n          // heap value, and bump its refcount (unguarded — a ref cell is always\\n          // heap) so the shared cell survives until BOTH the defining scope and\\n          // this closure have dropped it.\\n          emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n          emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n          emit_local_get(buf, __cap_resolve)\\n          emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n          emit_i64_or(buf)\\n          emit_i64_store(buf, 3, cap_off + csi * 8)\\n          emit_rc_word_inc_saturating(buf, () -> {\\n            emit_local_get(buf, __cap_resolve)\\n            emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n            emit_i32_const(buf, 4)\\n            emit_i32_sub(buf)\\n          })\\n        } else {\\n          emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n          emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n          emit_local_get(buf, __cap_resolve)\\n          emit_i64_store(buf, 3, cap_off + csi * 8)\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 0)\\n        emit_i64_store(buf, 3, cap_off + csi * 8)\\n      }\\n      csi = csi + 1\\n    }\\n    if ctx.enable_rc {\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 8)\\n      emit_i64_add(buf)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n      emit_i64_or(buf)\\n    } else {\\n      emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n      emit_i64_or(buf)\\n    }\\n    nl2\\n  }\\n}\\n\")\n}\n\nlet cli_adapter_source_68 = () -> (String, String) {\n  (\"vibe/compiler/codegen/expr/compile_call.vibe\",\n\"//# Imports\\n\\nimport .. / .. / builtin_name.vibe {\\n  canonical_builtin_name\\n}\\n\\nimport .. / .. / core {\\n  Expr, Pat, Stmt, TypeExpr, bytebuf_length, bytebuf_new, bytebuf_push, bytebuf_push_section, bytebuf_push_vec_header, bytebuf_to_bytes, leb128_encode_s64, leb128_encode_u32\\n}\\n\\nimport .. / common_analysis {\\n  collect_free_vars, collect_strings_stmts, emit_closure_call_tail, emit_closure_resolve, emit_i64_extend_i32_u, is_mut_captured_in\\n}\\n\\nimport .. / common_base {\\n  emit_rc_word_inc_saturating, CompileCtx, CtorTable, FuncTable, LambdaTable, StrTable, emit_rc_dup_guarded, effect_name_to_tag, effect_op_index, emit_binop_op, emit_box_float, emit_heap_grow_after_heap_set, emit_i32_eq, emit_i32_eqz, emit_i32_ge_u, emit_i32_gt_u, emit_i32_mul, emit_i32_ne, emit_i32_sub, emit_i64_load, emit_i64_store, emit_index_one, emit_str_ref, emit_unbox_float, expr_tag, get_arm_body, get_arm_pat, get_ebinop_op, get_efn_body, get_eif_cond, get_eif_else, get_eif_then, get_elet_body, get_elet_name, get_elet_val, get_slet_expr, get_slet_name, is_efn, is_eident, is_etuple, is_pbind, is_pbool, is_pctor, is_pint, is_pstring, is_ptuple, is_pwild, is_slet, lookup_ctor, resolve_func, resolve_local\\n}\\n\\nimport .. / common_extractors {\\n  array_contains_str, emit_assignop_op, emit_memory_copy, find_catchall_idx, get_earray_elems, get_eassign_body, get_eassign_name, get_eassign_val, get_eassignop_body, get_eassignop_name, get_eassignop_op, get_eassignop_val, get_ebinop_lhs, get_ebinop_rhs, get_ebool_value, get_ecall_args, get_ecall_callee, get_efloat_value, get_efn_params, get_eforin_body, get_eforin_iter, get_eforin_name, get_eident_name, get_eint_value, get_eletmut_body, get_eletmut_name, get_eletmut_val, get_eletrec_body, get_eletrec_name, get_eletrec_val, get_eseq_first, get_eseq_second, get_estring_value, get_ethrow_expr, get_etuple_elems, get_eunaryop_expr, get_eunaryop_op, get_ewhile_body, get_ewhile_cond, get_match_arms, get_match_scrutinee, get_pbind_name, get_pbool_value, get_pctor_args, get_pctor_name, get_pint_value, get_pstring_value, get_ptuple_pats, get_slet_export, str_table_lookup\\n}\\n\\nimport .. / wasm_emit {\\n  emit_block_i64, emit_block_void, emit_br, emit_br_if, emit_call, emit_call_indirect, emit_code_section, emit_code_section_with_locals, emit_data_section, emit_data_section_multi, emit_drop, emit_element_section_active, emit_else, emit_end, emit_export_section, emit_export_section_multi, emit_exports_full, emit_exports_with_memory, emit_f64_add, emit_f64_const_bits, emit_f64_convert_i64_s, emit_f64_div, emit_f64_eq, emit_f64_ge, emit_f64_gt, emit_f64_le, emit_f64_lt, emit_f64_mul, emit_f64_ne, emit_f64_neg, emit_f64_reinterpret_i64, emit_f64_sub, emit_func_type_raw, emit_function_section, emit_global_get, emit_global_section_i32_mut, emit_global_set, emit_header, emit_i32_add, emit_i32_const, emit_i32_load, emit_i32_load8_u, emit_i32_store, emit_i32_store8, emit_i32_wrap_i64, emit_i64_add, emit_i64_and, emit_i64_const, emit_i64_div_s, emit_i64_eq, emit_i64_eqz, emit_i64_extend_i32_s, emit_i64_ge_s, emit_i64_gt_s, emit_i64_le_s, emit_i64_lt_s, emit_i64_mul, emit_i64_ne, emit_i64_or, emit_i64_reinterpret_f64, emit_i64_rem_s, emit_i64_shl, emit_i64_shr_s, emit_i64_sub, emit_i64_trunc_f64_s, emit_i64_xor, emit_if_i64, emit_if_void, emit_import_section_func, emit_local_get, emit_local_set, emit_local_tee, emit_loop_void, emit_memory_section, emit_name, emit_return, emit_table_section_funcref, emit_type_section, emit_type_section_multi, string_to_data, emit_v128_load, emit_v128_store, emit_i8x16_splat, emit_i8x16_eq, emit_i8x16_le_u, emit_i8x16_ge_u, emit_v128_and, emit_v128_or, emit_v128_not, emit_i8x16_bitmask, emit_v128_any_true, emit_i8x16_all_true, emit_v128_const_splat_byte\\n}\\n\\nimport ./compile_lambda.vibe {\\n  compile_lambda\\n}\\n\\nimport ./compile_match.vibe {\\n  compile_match\\n}\\n\\n//# Functions\\n\\n// A field projection `a.f` (EDot) passed as an argument to an owning user\\n// function (which drops its parameters) is a borrow of the source aggregate.\\n// Without a retain the callee's param-drop frees it while the source still\\n// references it — a double-free that corrupts the free list (e.g. derived\\n// `T::equals` passing `a.items` to the consuming `__arr_equals__` helper, #704).\\n// Perceus emits no action for bare projections, so this guarded dup is the only\\n// owner-increment. Scalars are no-ops; this is NOT applied to borrow-arg0\\n// builtins (Array::get/length etc.), which do not drop their argument.\\nlet cc_is_projection: (Expr) -> Bool = (e) -> {\\n  match e {\\n    EDot(_, _, _) => true,\\n    _ => false\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// #705: a borrow-RETURNING builtin call (`Array::get` / `Map::get` / `__index`)\\n// yields a borrowed view of a heap element — its refcount is NOT bumped, like a\\n// projection `a.f`. When that result is consumed in an OWNING position (a ctor\\n// field, or an owning call arg of a fn that drops its params), it must be\\n// rc_dup'd or the container's recursive drop and the consume double-free the\\n// same element (e.g. `chk(Array::get(ps, i))` recursing over a heap array, or\\n// `validate(s, Map::get(obj, key))`). Scalars are even so the guarded dup is a\\n// runtime no-op for `Array[Int]` etc.\\nexport let cc_is_borrow_ret_call: (Expr, CompileCtx) -> Bool = (e, ctx) -> {\\n  match e {\\n    ECall(callee, _, _) =>\\n    match callee {\\n      EIdent(f, _) => f == \\\"Array::get\\\" || f == \\\"Map::get\\\" || f == \\\"__index\\\" || f == \\\"__rec_field\\\" || array_contains_str(ctx.borrow_ret_names, f),\\n      _ => false\\n    },\\n    _ => false\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Is `e` provably a scalar (Int/Bool) by structure alone — an int/bool literal,\\n// a bitwise/shift/comparison/logical binop, or a logical `!`? Conservative: no\\n// ident-slot/type lookup and no arith ops (+,-,*,/ can be Float). Used to route\\n// an explicit `eq(a, b)` to a direct i64.eq when an operand is provably scalar,\\n// matching how the `==` binop dispatches intish operands (emit_eq_value). Without\\n// this, `eq(int, int)` falls through to the generic bound `eq` whose\\n// `looks_like_string`/str_eq fallback reads OOB on ints resembling fat-pointers\\n// (#678 residual) — e.g. leb128's `eq(val, 0)` trapped under RC (#705).\\nlet rec cc_arg_is_scalarish: (Expr) -> Bool with { Error } = (e) -> {\\n  let t = expr_tag(e)\\n  if t == 0 || t == 1 {\\n    true\\n  } else if t == 5 {\\n    let op = get_ebinop_op(e)\\n    op == \\\"&\\\" || op == \\\"|\\\" || op == \\\"^\\\" || op == \\\"<<\\\" || op == \\\">>\\\" || op == \\\"%\\\" || op == \\\"<\\\" || op == \\\">\\\" || op == \\\"<=\\\" || op == \\\">=\\\" || op == \\\"==\\\" || op == \\\"!=\\\" || op == \\\"&&\\\" || op == \\\"||\\\"\\n  } else if t == 6 {\\n    let uop = get_eunaryop_op(e)\\n    // `!x` is Bool; `-x` is scalar iff its operand is (so a negative int literal\\n    // like `-1`, which parses as unary minus of `1`, is detected as scalar).\\n    uop == \\\"!\\\" || (uop == \\\"-\\\" && cc_arg_is_scalarish(get_eunaryop_expr(e)))\\n  } else {\\n    false\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// #706: is `e` a bare reference to a value live-in to an enclosing loop (and not\\n// a `mut` ref-cell, whose reassignment already manages its own drop)? Passing\\n// such a value to a consuming (owning) parameter inside the loop frees it on the\\n// first iteration; dup'ing at the call site keeps the loop-carried reference\\n// alive across the back-edge. rc_dup is a no-op on scalars, so a scalar loop var\\n// caught here costs only a wasted (guarded) dup, not a correctness problem.\\nexport let cc_is_loop_borrowed_ident: (Expr, CompileCtx) -> Bool = (e, ctx) -> {\\n  match e {\\n    EIdent(name, _) =>\\n    array_contains_str(ctx.loop_borrowed_names, name) && !array_contains_str(ctx.ref_cell_names, name),\\n    _ => false\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// Builtins whose arg0 is BORROWED (read in place, not consumed/dropped). Kept in\\n// sync with `is_borrow_arg0_call` in perceus/index.vibe — a projection passed as\\n// arg0 to one of these must NOT be rc_dup'd at the call site (the callee never\\n// drops it, so the dup would leak; #704). Other argument positions are owning.\\nlet cc_is_borrow_arg0_call: (String) -> Bool = (f) -> {\\n  f == \\\"__index\\\" || f == \\\"Array::get\\\" || f == \\\"Array::length\\\" || f == \\\"Array::set\\\" || f == \\\"Array::push\\\" || f == \\\"ArrayBuilder::push\\\" || f == \\\"StringBuilder::push\\\" || f == \\\"MapBuilder::set\\\" || f == \\\"Map::get\\\" || f == \\\"Map::keys\\\" || f == \\\"Map::has_key\\\" || f == \\\"Map::set\\\" || f == \\\"Bytes::push\\\" || f == \\\"Bytes::set\\\" || f == \\\"Bytes::get\\\" || f == \\\"Bytes::length\\\" || f == \\\"__rec_field\\\"\\n}\\n\\n// #664/#678: is `e` statically — BY SHAPE — a known integer that must NOT be run\\n// through `__to_string`'s string-pointer heuristic (which misreads a large int\\n// as an empty string)? An Int literal, or a bitwise/shift/mod expression (those\\n// operators are never float or string). Bare idents are deliberately excluded:\\n// a per-slot \\\"is int\\\" log is unsound because slots are reused across scopes\\n// without updating it. Covers `\\\"\\\\{1 << 40}\\\"` and integer-literal interpolation.\\nlet ts_known_int: (Expr, Array[String], CompileCtx) -> Bool = (e, local_names, ctx) -> {\\n  let tag = expr_tag(e)\\n  if tag == 0 {\\n    true\\n  } else if tag == 5 {\\n    let op = get_ebinop_op(e)\\n    op == \\\"&\\\" || op == \\\"|\\\" || op == \\\"^\\\" || op == \\\"<<\\\" || op == \\\">>\\\" || op == \\\"%\\\"\\n  } else {\\n    false\\n  }\\n}\\n\\nexport let compile_call: (Bytes, Expr, Array[Expr], Array[String], Int, CompileCtx, Int, (Bytes, Expr, Array[String], Int, CompileCtx, Int) -> Int with { Error }) -> Int with { Error } = (buf, callee, args, local_names, next_local, ctx, ld, ce) -> {\\n  if is_eident(callee) {\\n    let fname0 = canonical_builtin_name(get_eident_name(callee))\\n    // Stream[T] (docs/spec/wasi-p3-async.md §2.4) is backed by the eager Array\\n    // machinery on the linear backend: map/fold reuse the existing inline\\n    // Array::map / Array::fold lowering verbatim (same arg order, same value\\n    // representation). empty/once/filter are handled explicitly below.\\n    let fname = if fname0 == \\\"Stream::map\\\" {\\n      \\\"Array::map\\\"\\n    } else if fname0 == \\\"Stream::fold\\\" {\\n      \\\"Array::fold\\\"\\n    } else {\\n      fname0\\n    }\\n    let fn_len2 = Array::length(ctx.func_table.names)\\n    let mut fn_idx_in_list = -1\\n    let mut __tr_j = 0\\n    while __tr_j < fn_len2 {\\n      if Array::get(ctx.func_table.names, __tr_j) == fname {\\n        fn_idx_in_list = __tr_j\\n        __tr_j = fn_len2\\n      } else {\\n        __tr_j = __tr_j + 1\\n      }\\n    }\\n    let mut local_idx_hint = -1\\n    let mut li = Array::length(local_names) - 1\\n    while li >= 0 {\\n      if Array::get(local_names, li) == fname {\\n        local_idx_hint = li\\n        li = -1\\n      } else {\\n        li = li - 1\\n      }\\n    }\\n    let prefer_bound_call = fn_idx_in_list >= 0 || local_idx_hint >= 0\\n    let ctor_lookup_idx = lookup_ctor(ctx.ctor_table.names, fname, 0)\\n    if ctor_lookup_idx >= 0 {\\n      let tag = Array::get(ctx.ctor_table.tags, ctor_lookup_idx)\\n      let fc = Array::get(ctx.ctor_table.field_counts, ctor_lookup_idx)\\n      let ptr_local = next_local\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__ctor_ptr\\\")\\n      let actual_args = if Array::length(args) == 1 {\\n        match Array::get(args, 0) {\\n          ERecord(rec_fields) => {\\n            let mut si2 = 0\\n            let mut sn_idx = -1\\n            while si2 < Array::length(ctx.ctor_table.struct_names) {\\n              if Array::get(ctx.ctor_table.struct_names, si2) == fname {\\n                sn_idx = si2\\n                si2 = Array::length(ctx.ctor_table.struct_names)\\n              } else {\\n                si2 = si2 + 1\\n              }\\n            }\\n            if sn_idx >= 0 {\\n              let def_fnames = Array::get(ctx.ctor_table.struct_field_names, sn_idx)\\n              let ordered = Array::slice([\\n                EUnit\\n              ], 0, 0)\\n              let mut oi = 0\\n              while oi < Array::length(def_fnames) {\\n                let target_name = Array::get(def_fnames, oi)\\n                let mut ri = 0\\n                let mut found_rfv = EUnit\\n                while ri < Array::length(rec_fields) {\\n                  let (rfn, rfv) = Array::get(rec_fields, ri)\\n                  if rfn == target_name {\\n                    found_rfv = rfv\\n                    ri = Array::length(rec_fields)\\n                  } else {\\n                    ri = ri + 1\\n                  }\\n                }\\n                Array::push(ordered, found_rfv)\\n                oi = oi + 1\\n              }\\n              ordered\\n            } else {\\n              args\\n            }\\n          },\\n          _ => args\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        args\\n      }\\n      if ctx.enable_rc {\\n        let total = 16 + fc * 8\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, total)\\n        emit_call(buf, ctx.rc_alloc_func_idx)\\n        emit_local_set(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, total)\\n        emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 0)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 4)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i32_store8(buf, 0, 7)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, tag)\\n        emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 8)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, fc)\\n        emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 12)\\n        let mut nl_c = next_local + 1\\n        let mut fi_c = 0\\n        while fi_c < Array::length(actual_args) {\\n          let carg_c = Array::get(actual_args, fi_c)\\n          nl_c = ce(buf, carg_c, local_names, nl_c, ctx, ld)\\n          let val_local = nl_c\\n          Array::push(local_names, \\\"__ctor_val\\\")\\n          emit_local_set(buf, val_local)\\n          nl_c = nl_c + 1\\n          // A heap field projection `a.f` stored into a constructor is a borrow;\\n          // the constructed value OWNS its fields (drop class 1 recurses), so\\n          // retain it or the source's drop double-frees it (e.g. `Some(b.items)`\\n          // returned while `b` is dropped). Mirrors the ERecord field-store dup\\n          // (#704). Perceus emits no action for bare projections.\\n          // #715: also retain a bare-ident arg whose binding is borrow-bound or\\n          // loop-borrowed (cc_is_loop_borrowed_ident) -- same gap as the ETuple\\n          // case in compile_expr_tail2.vibe (see the comment there).\\n          if ctx.enable_rc && (cc_is_projection(carg_c) || cc_is_borrow_ret_call(carg_c, ctx) || cc_is_loop_borrowed_ident(carg_c, ctx)) {\\n            emit_rc_dup_guarded(buf, val_local, ctx.rc_shadow)\\n          } else {\\n            ()\\n          }\\n          emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n          emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n          emit_local_get(buf, val_local)\\n          emit_i64_store(buf, 3, 16 + fi_c * 8)\\n          fi_c = fi_c + 1\\n        }\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 8)\\n        emit_i64_add(buf)\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i64_or(buf)\\n        nl_c\\n      } else {\\n        let obj_size = 8 + fc * 8\\n        emit_global_get(buf, 0)\\n        emit_i64_extend_i32_u(buf)\\n        emit_local_set(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_global_get(buf, 0)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, obj_size)\\n        emit_i32_add(buf)\\n        emit_global_set(buf, 0)\\n        emit_heap_grow_after_heap_set(buf, ctx)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, tag)\\n        emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 0)\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n        emit_i32_const(buf, fc)\\n        emit_i32_store(buf, 2, 4)\\n        let mut nl_c = next_local + 1\\n        let mut fi_c = 0\\n        while fi_c < Array::length(actual_args) {\\n          nl_c = ce(buf, Array::get(actual_args, fi_c), local_names, nl_c, ctx, ld)\\n          let val_local = nl_c\\n          Array::push(local_names, \\\"__ctor_val\\\")\\n          emit_local_set(buf, val_local)\\n          nl_c = nl_c + 1\\n          emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n          emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n          emit_local_get(buf, val_local)\\n          emit_i64_store(buf, 3, 8 + fi_c * 8)\\n          fi_c = fi_c + 1\\n        }\\n        emit_local_get(buf, ptr_local)\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i64_or(buf)\\n        nl_c\\n      }\\n    }\\n    else if fname == \\\"eq\\\" && Array::length(args) == 2 && (!prefer_bound_call || cc_arg_is_scalarish(Array::get(args, 0)) || cc_arg_is_scalarish(Array::get(args, 1))) {\\n      // Direct i64.eq for `eq(a, b)` when it is the builtin and at least one\\n      // operand is provably scalar. This sidesteps the bound `eq`'s string\\n      // fallback, which reads OOB on Int values resembling fat-pointers (#705):\\n      // `==` already dispatches intish operands this way via emit_eq_value, and\\n      // `eq` must match. A genuinely string/heap `eq` (no scalar operand) still\\n      // falls through to the bound call below.\\n      //\\n      // #710/#711: keeping the scalarish disjunct (not just !prefer_bound_call)\\n      // is required -- prefer_bound_call is a global cross-file name match, not\\n      // scoped to the calling file (see #711), so dropping it regressed\\n      // leb128_test.vibe. Root fix tracked in #711.\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_i64_eq(buf)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_s(buf)\\n      // ADR-0055: under RC a Bool is a TAGGED scalar (true = 1<<1). The raw\\n      // i64.eq result is 0/1 (untagged); tag it so `eq(..) == true`/`if`/derived\\n      // comparisons see the same representation as a bool literal (#705 — without\\n      // this, `eq(a,b) == true` compared untagged 1 against tagged 2 and failed).\\n      // The bump backend leaves bools untagged, so only shift under RC.\\n      if ctx.enable_rc {\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i64_shl(buf)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"not\\\" {\\n      let nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_i64_eqz(buf)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_s(buf)\\n      if ctx.enable_rc {\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i64_shl(buf)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"await\\\" {\\n      // M1b-3b (docs/spec/wasi-p3-async.md): awaiting a ready future yields the\\n      // value directly (ready-future fast path). Real blocking future.read for\\n      // async sources (host async imports / spawned subtasks) is M1b-3c.\\n      ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Future::ready\\\" {\\n      // Future::ready(x) carries x directly — no canon future is created for an\\n      // already-resolved value.\\n      ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Task::spawn\\\" {\\n      // Structured concurrency, synchronous model (docs/spec/wasi-p3-async.md\\n      // §2.5): on the single-threaded linear backend a spawned task runs its\\n      // thunk eagerly, so the Task[T] value *is* the resolved result. `join`\\n      // is then identity and `cancel` a no-op. Real subtask spawn over\\n      // waitable-set / future.cancel is documented future work.\\n      let nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      let fn_l = nl\\n      let slot_l = nl + 1\\n      let env_l = nl + 2\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__spawn_fn\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__spawn_slot\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__spawn_env\\\")\\n      emit_local_set(buf, fn_l)\\n      emit_closure_resolve(buf, fn_l, slot_l, env_l)\\n      emit_closure_call_tail(buf, env_l, slot_l, 9, 0)\\n      nl + 3\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Task::join\\\" {\\n      // The task already holds its resolved value (eager spawn) — join is the\\n      // identity projection onto that value.\\n      ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Task::cancel\\\" {\\n      // The eager task has already completed; cancel evaluates the handle for\\n      // its effects, drops it, and yields Unit.\\n      let nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_drop(buf)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 0)\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Task::race\\\" {\\n      // Both tasks are already resolved under the eager model; race resolves to\\n      // the first task's value. (b is evaluated for its effects, then dropped.)\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_drop(buf)\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Stream::empty\\\" {\\n      // Empty stream = empty backing array.\\n      let (arr_new_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"array_new\\\")\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_new_fi)\\n      next_local\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Stream::once\\\" {\\n      // Singleton stream = one-element backing array.\\n      let (arr_new_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"array_new\\\")\\n      let (arr_push_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"Array::push\\\")\\n      let nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      let val_l = nl\\n      let arr_l = nl + 1\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__once_val\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__once_arr\\\")\\n      emit_local_set(buf, val_l)\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_new_fi)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, arr_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, arr_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, val_l)\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_push_fi)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, arr_l)\\n      nl + 2\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Stream::filter\\\" {\\n      // Eager filter: walk the backing array, keep elements whose predicate is\\n      // truthy. Mirrors the Array::map loop but pushes conditionally.\\n      let (arr_new_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"array_new\\\")\\n      let (arr_len_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"Array::length\\\")\\n      let (arr_get_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"Array::get\\\")\\n      let (arr_push_fi, _, _) = resolve_func(ctx.func_table, \\\"Array::push\\\")\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      let arr_l = nl\\n      let fn_l = nl + 1\\n      let res_l = nl + 2\\n      let len_l = nl + 3\\n      let i_l = nl + 4\\n      let slot_l = nl + 5\\n      let env_l = nl + 6\\n      let elem_l = nl + 7\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_arr\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_fn\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_res\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_len\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_i\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_slot\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_env\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__filter_elem\\\")\\n      emit_local_set(buf, fn_l)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, arr_l)\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_new_fi)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, res_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, arr_l)\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_len_fi)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, len_l)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 0)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, i_l)\\n      emit_closure_resolve(buf, fn_l, slot_l, env_l)\\n      emit_block_void(buf)\\n      emit_loop_void(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, i_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, len_l)\\n      emit_i64_ge_s(buf)\\n      emit_br_if(buf, 1)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, arr_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, i_l)\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_get_fi)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, elem_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, elem_l)\\n      emit_closure_call_tail(buf, env_l, slot_l, 9, 1)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 0)\\n      emit_i64_ne(buf)\\n      emit_if_void(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, res_l)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, elem_l)\\n      emit_call(buf, arr_push_fi)\\n      emit_end(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, i_l)\\n      emit_index_one(buf, ctx)\\n      emit_i64_add(buf)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, i_l)\\n      emit_br(buf, 0)\\n      emit_end(buf)\\n      emit_end(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, res_l)\\n      nl + 8\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Stream::next\\\" {\\n      // Stream::next(s) : Future[Option[T]] (docs/spec §2.4). On the eager\\n      // Array-backed model `next` peeks the head: Some(s[0]) if non-empty else\\n      // None. Synthesize the Option expression and reuse the existing ctor +\\n      // Array::length/get lowering via `ce`. (await unwraps the ready future.)\\n      let s_expr = Array::get(args, 0)\\n      let synth = ELet(\\\"__nx_s\\\", s_expr, EIf(ECall(EIdent(\\\"lt\\\", -1), [\\n        EInt(0),\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"Array::length\\\", -1), [\\n          EIdent(\\\"__nx_s\\\", -1)\\n        ], -1)\\n      ], -1), ECall(EIdent(\\\"Some\\\", -1), [\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"Array::get\\\", -1), [\\n          EIdent(\\\"__nx_s\\\", -1),\\n          EInt(0)\\n        ], -1)\\n      ], -1), ECall(EIdent(\\\"None\\\", -1), Array::slice([\\n        EUnit\\n      ], 0, 0), -1)))\\n      ce(buf, synth, local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Task::timeout\\\" {\\n      // Task::timeout(ms, thunk) : Option[T] (docs/spec §2.5). Synchronous eager\\n      // model: the thunk always completes, so the result is Some(thunk()); the\\n      // deadline is evaluated for its effects then ignored. Synthesized and\\n      // lowered via `ce` so the Some ctor + 0-arg closure call reuse existing\\n      // lowering.\\n      let ms_expr = Array::get(args, 0)\\n      let thunk_expr = Array::get(args, 1)\\n      let synth = ELet(\\\"__to_fn\\\", thunk_expr, ELet(\\\"__to_ms\\\", ms_expr, ECall(EIdent(\\\"Some\\\", -1), [\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"__to_fn\\\", -1), Array::slice([\\n          EUnit\\n        ], 0, 0), -1)\\n      ], -1)))\\n      ce(buf, synth, local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"String::to_bytes\\\" {\\n      // String::to_bytes(s) : Stream[Int]  (ByteStream, docs/spec §2.4/§4.1).\\n      // Eagerly materialise the string's bytes into the Array that backs a\\n      // Stream[Int], so request/response bodies can be consumed with the Stream\\n      // combinators. Synthesized as a `let mut arr = []; while i < length(s) {\\n      // Array::push(arr, char_code_at(s, i)); i = i + 1 }; arr` loop and lowered\\n      // via `ce`, so String::length/char_code_at + the loop counter follow the\\n      // same (RC) tagging conventions as ordinary source. char_code_at reads one\\n      // byte (i32.load8_u), so this is byte-accurate.\\n      let s_expr = Array::get(args, 0)\\n      let loop_body = ESeq(ECall(EIdent(\\\"Array::push\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__tb_arr\\\", -1),\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"String::char_code_at\\\", -1), [\\n          EIdent(\\\"__tb_s\\\", -1),\\n          EIdent(\\\"__tb_i\\\", -1)\\n        ], -1)\\n      ], -1), EAssign(\\\"__tb_i\\\", ECall(EIdent(\\\"add\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__tb_i\\\", -1),\\n        EInt(1)\\n      ], -1), EUnit))\\n      let synth = ELet(\\\"__tb_s\\\", s_expr, ELetMut(\\\"__tb_arr\\\", EArray(Array::slice([\\n        EUnit\\n      ], 0, 0)), ELetMut(\\\"__tb_i\\\", EInt(0), ESeq(EWhile(ECall(EIdent(\\\"lt\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__tb_i\\\", -1),\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"String::length\\\", -1), [\\n          EIdent(\\\"__tb_s\\\", -1)\\n        ], -1)\\n      ], -1), loop_body), EIdent(\\\"__tb_arr\\\", -1)))))\\n      ce(buf, synth, local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"Stream::to_string\\\" {\\n      // Stream::to_string(bs) : String  (ByteStream -> String, docs/spec\\n      // §M2c-2). Collect a Stream[Int] of byte codes into a String, e.g. to\\n      // build a response body. Synthesized as `let parts = []; while i <\\n      // length(bs) { Array::push(parts, String::from_char_code(bs[i])); i = i +\\n      // 1 }; String::join(parts, \\\"\\\")` and lowered via `ce`. Pushing one-char\\n      // pieces and joining once is O(n); the earlier `acc = String::concat(acc,\\n      // ...)` accumulator was O(n^2) (each concat copied the whole prefix), the\\n      // dominant cost in the streaming bench (4 KB to_string: 1.77s -> see\\n      // scripts/bench_streaming.sh). linked_compile always seeds \\\"\\\" into the\\n      // string table, so the join separator literal resolves.\\n      let bs_expr = Array::get(args, 0)\\n      let ts_body = ESeq(ECall(EIdent(\\\"Array::push\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__ts_parts\\\", -1),\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"String::from_char_code\\\", -1), [\\n          ECall(EIdent(\\\"Array::get\\\", -1), [\\n            EIdent(\\\"__ts_arr\\\", -1),\\n            EIdent(\\\"__ts_i\\\", -1)\\n          ], -1)\\n        ], -1)\\n      ], -1), EAssign(\\\"__ts_i\\\", ECall(EIdent(\\\"add\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__ts_i\\\", -1),\\n        EInt(1)\\n      ], -1), EUnit))\\n      let synth = ELet(\\\"__ts_arr\\\", bs_expr, ELetMut(\\\"__ts_parts\\\", EArray(Array::slice([\\n        EUnit\\n      ], 0, 0)), ELetMut(\\\"__ts_i\\\", EInt(0), ESeq(EWhile(ECall(EIdent(\\\"lt\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__ts_i\\\", -1),\\n        ECall(EIdent(\\\"Array::length\\\", -1), [\\n          EIdent(\\\"__ts_arr\\\", -1)\\n        ], -1)\\n      ], -1), ts_body), ECall(EIdent(\\\"String::join\\\", -1), [\\n        EIdent(\\\"__ts_parts\\\", -1),\\n        EString(\\\"\\\")\\n      ], -1)))))\\n      ce(buf, synth, local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"add\\\" {\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_i64_add(buf)\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"sub\\\" {\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_i64_sub(buf)\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"mul\\\" {\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_i64_mul(buf)\\n      // Under RC, Int values are tagged `(n << 1)`. Multiplying two tagged\\n      // operands raw gives `(a*b) << 2` (an extra factor of 2 vs. the `<< 1`\\n      // every other Int carries) -- shift right once to correct back, exactly\\n      // like the `*` EBinOp path does (compile_expr.vibe `op == \\\"*\\\"`) that\\n      // this builtin fast path duplicates but had not mirrored.\\n      if ctx.enable_rc {\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i64_shr_s(buf)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"lt\\\" {\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      emit_i64_lt_s(buf)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_s(buf)\\n      // Under RC, Bool values are also tagged `(0|1) << 1` (mirrors the `<`\\n      // EBinOp path's retag) -- untagged here means callers see 0 (== false\\n      // tagged) but a true result reads as 1 instead of the expected 2.\\n      if ctx.enable_rc {\\n        emit_i64_const(buf, 1)\\n        emit_i64_shl(buf)\\n      } else {\\n        ()\\n      }\\n      nl\\n    }\\n    else if !prefer_bound_call && fname == \\\"simd_skip_ws\\\" {\\n      // #536 Phase 3: fused SIMD whitespace skip.\\n      // simd_skip_ws(src: Bytes, pos: Int, len: Int) -> Int returns the first\\n      // index >= pos that is NOT ASCII whitespace (' ' \\\\t \\\\n \\\\r), or len if all\\n      // remaining bytes are whitespace. Scans 16 bytes at a time with the v128\\n      // chunk kept on the operand stack (NO heap boxing — the per-op boxed v128\\n      // intrinsics would bump-allocate 16 bytes each and leak), plus a scalar\\n      // tail. Bytes layout (gen_bytes_get_body): [alloc@0][len@4][payload_ptr@8].\\n      let mut nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 0), local_names, next_local, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 1), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      nl = ce(buf, Array::get(args, 2), local_names, nl, ctx, ld)\\n      let base_l = nl\\n      let pos_l = nl + 1\\n      let len_l = nl + 2\\n      let res_l = nl + 3\\n      let mask_l = nl + 4\\n      let addr_l = nl + 5\\n      let b_l = nl + 6\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_base\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_pos\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_len\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_res\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_mask\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_addr\\\")\\n      Array::push(local_names, \\\"__sw_b\\\")\\n      // stack: srcval, posval, lenval\\n      emit_local_set(buf, len_l)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, pos_l)\\n      // top = srcval; base = payload_ptr (i32 @ +8) extended to i64\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_load(buf, 2, 8)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_u(buf)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, base_l)\\n      // res defaults to len (every path overwrites it; keep it defined)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, len_l)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, res_l)\\n      emit_block_void(buf)\\n      // $ret\\n      emit_block_void(buf)\\n      // $tail\\n      emit_loop_void(buf)\\n      // $scan: if (pos + 16 > len) br $tail\\n      emit_local_get(buf, pos_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_const(buf, 16)\\n      emit_i32_add(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, len_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_gt_u(buf)\\n      emit_if_void(buf)\\n      emit_br(buf, 2)\\n      emit_end(buf)\\n      // addr = base + pos\\n      emit_local_get(buf, base_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, pos_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_add(buf)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_u(buf)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, addr_l)\\n      // is_ws = (c==0x20) | (c==0x09) | (c==0x0A) | (c==0x0D), v128 on stack\\n      emit_local_get(buf, addr_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_v128_load(buf, 0, 0)\\n      emit_v128_const_splat_byte(buf, 32)\\n      emit_i8x16_eq(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, addr_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_v128_load(buf, 0, 0)\\n      emit_v128_const_splat_byte(buf, 9)\\n      emit_i8x16_eq(buf)\\n      emit_v128_or(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, addr_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_v128_load(buf, 0, 0)\\n      emit_v128_const_splat_byte(buf, 10)\\n      emit_i8x16_eq(buf)\\n      emit_v128_or(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, addr_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_v128_load(buf, 0, 0)\\n      emit_v128_const_splat_byte(buf, 13)\\n      emit_i8x16_eq(buf)\\n      emit_v128_or(buf)\\n      // mask = bitmask(not(is_ws)): bit i set => lane i is NON-whitespace\\n      emit_v128_not(buf)\\n      emit_i8x16_bitmask(buf)\\n      emit_i64_extend_i32_u(buf)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, mask_l)\\n      // if (mask == 0) { pos += 16; br $scan }\\n      emit_local_get(buf, mask_l)\\n      emit_i32_wrap_i64(buf)\\n      emit_i32_eqz(buf)\\n      emit_if_void(buf)\\n      emit_local_get(buf, pos_l)\\n      emit_i64_const(buf, 16)\\n      emit_i64_add(buf)\\n      emit_local_set(buf, pos_l)\\n      emit_br(buf, 1)\\n      emit_end(buf)\\n      // found: